{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"2205","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"E. Simons and Dividing the Rhythm"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"2 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"512 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"I grip my troubles within my hand, then hurl them off a thousand lands."}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"container"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"— SHUN, "},{"children":[{"attrs":{"href":"https://open.spotify.com/track/0ZOaDlRReh6qeZWipAMHDu"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"ONMYWAY"}],"kind":"link"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"container"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Consider that Simons is given an array $$$a$$$ of size $$$m$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Simons must operate on the array "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"exactly once"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" as follows:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" First, he has to select an integer $$$k$$$ and choose $$$k$$$ pairs of integers $$$[l_1,r_1],[l_2,r_2],\\ldots,[l_k,r_k]$$$, such that: "},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"kind":"list"}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$l_i\\le r_i$$$ for each $$$1\\le i\\le k$$$, "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$l_1=1$$$, $$$r_k=m$$$, and "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$r_i+1=l_{i+1}$$$ for each $$$i$$$ from $$$1$$$ to $$$k-1$$$. "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" Then, he reverses each subarray $$$[a_{l_i},a_{l_i+1},\\ldots, a_{r_i}]$$$ independently. After this, the array will become $$$[a_{r_1},a_{r_1-1},\\ldots,a_{l_1},a_{r_2},\\ldots,a_{l_{k-1}},a_{r_{k}},a_{r_k-1},\\ldots,a_{l_k}]$$$. "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"You are given an array $$$T$$$ of size $$$n$$$. Count the number of arrays $$$S$$$ such that Simons can transform $$$S$$$ to $$$T$$$, modulo $$$998\\,244\\,353$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Each test contains multiple test cases. The first line contains the number of test cases $$$t$$$ ($$$1 \\le t \\le 8000$$$). The description of the test cases follows. "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line contains an integer $$$n$$$ ($$$1\\le n\\le 8000$$$) — the length of $$$T$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The second line contains $$$n$$$ integers $$$T_1,T_2,\\ldots,T_n$$$ ($$$1\\le T_i\\le 8000$$$) — the elements of $$$T$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"It is guaranteed that the sum of $$$n$$$ over all test cases does not exceed $$$8000$$$. "}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For each test case, output a single integer — the number of arrays $$$S$$$, modulo $$$998\\,244\\,353$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Example"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n5\n4\n1 1 2 1\n4\n1 2 3 1\n6\n1 3 2 3 3 2\n10\n2 3 1 4 3 1 4 3 1 2\n1\n8000\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n4\n7\n22\n383\n1\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the first test case, we can see only the following arrays can be transformed to $$$T$$$:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" For $$$S=[2,1,1,1]$$$, Simons will choose $$$[1,3]$$$ and $$$[4,4]$$$. Thus, the array will become $$$[1,1,2,1]$$$, equal to $$$T$$$. "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" For $$$S=[1,2,1,1]$$$, Simons will choose $$$[1,4]$$$. "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" For $$$S=[1,1,2,1]$$$, Simons will choose $$$[1,2]$$$, $$$[3,3]$$$, and $$$[4,4]$$$. "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" For $$$S=[1,1,1,2]$$$, Simons will choose $$$[1,2]$$$ and $$$[3,4]$$$. "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the second test case, we can see only the following arrays can be transformed to $$$T$$$:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" For $$$S=[1,1,3,2]$$$, Simons will choose $$$[1,1]$$$ and $$$[2,4]$$$. "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" For $$$S=[1,2,1,3]$$$, Simons will choose $$$[1,1]$$$, $$$[2,2]$$$, and $$$[3,4]$$$. "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" For $$$S=[1,2,3,1]$$$, Simons will choose $$$[1,1]$$$, $$$[2,2]$$$, $$$[3,3]$$$, and $$$[4,4]$$$. "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" For $$$S=[1,3,2,1]$$$, Simons will choose $$$[1,4]$$$. "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" For $$$S=[2,1,1,3]$$$, Simons will choose $$$[1,2]$$$ and $$$[3,4]$$$. "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" For $$$S=[2,1,3,1]$$$, Simons will choose $$$[1,2]$$$, $$$[3,3]$$$, and $$$[4,4]$$$. "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" For $$$S=[3,2,1,1]$$$, Simons will choose $$$[1,3]$$$ and $$$[4,4]$$$. "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"E","problemCode":"2205E","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/2205/problem/E"}